\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Win for Anti- \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Clinic In Ruling on Donor Records\b0\par\par\uc2 By Abbie VanSickle \par \uc2 526 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 April 2026\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 17\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A crisis pregnancy group had asked the justices to allow it to sue in federal court over a demand for donor information by New Jersey officials.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court on Wednesday agreed that a New Jersey anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic should be able to challenge a subpoena issued by state officials seeking donor information.\par \par \uc2 In a unanimous decision written by Justice \uc2 Neil M. Gorsuch\uc2 , the justices cleared the way for First Choice Women's Resource Centers to bring a First Amendment challenge in federal court as it tries to fight the subpoena.\par \par \uc2 The ruling is a victory for the group, which alleged it had been targeted by state investigators because it sought to discourage women from having abortions. The New Jersey Office of the Attorney General has said the subpoena was part of an investigation into whether the group had misled potential clients and donors into thinking it offered abortions.\par \par \uc2 Justice Gorsuch wrote that ''since the 1950s, this court has confronted one official demand after another like the attorney general's'' and ''over and again, we have held those demands burden the exercise of First Amendment rights.''\par \par \uc2 The question before the justices was a technical one -- whether the group must first go through a process to challenge the subpoena in state court before bringing a First Amendment challenge in federal court. The justices agreed the group had already suffered an injury and could proceed in its federal lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Although the case did not squarely focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, it unfolded against the backdrop of the Supreme Court's 2022 decision to overturn Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 The year after the court's conservative supermajority ended the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , New Jersey's attorney general at the time, Matthew J. Platkin, issued an investigative subpoena, seeking donor information from First Choice Women's Resource Centers.\par \par \uc2 The organization brought a challenge in federal court, arguing that the effort to seek fund-raising information had a chilling effect on the group's First Amendment rights. Lawyers for the group argued in court filings that the attorney general had ''made no secret of his hostility toward pregnancy centers,'' calling the subpoena ''invasive.''\par \par \uc2 Lower courts found that the group's legal challenge was premature because the subpoena had not yet been ordered to go into effect by a state judge. The anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  centers then asked the Supreme Court to intervene and clear the way for the federal challenge.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration weighed in to support the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  centers, urging the justices to allow the group to challenge the subpoena and calling the case ''simple'' because the centers would face ''concrete injuries'' should they potentially have to turn over the records.\par \par \uc2 The dispute led to some unusual alliances before the court. \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  filed a friend-of-the-court brief in support of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  centers, asserting that ''a subpoena seeking sensitive donor information can chill a disfavored speaker's protected associations long before it's ever enforced,'' leading to ''chilling protected speech and association before the government lifts a finger.''\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020260430em4u0004h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
