\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Trump Widens  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rule For Recipients Of Foreign Aid\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael Crowley \par \uc2 697 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2026\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 13\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The change, which could affect more than $30 billion in foreign assistance, is the Trump administration's latest move against what the president calls ''woke ideology.''\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration will expand the ''Mexico City rule,'' which bars recipients of United States foreign aid from promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to include a ban on diversity, equity and inclusion policies or ''radical gender ideologies,'' Vice President \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  announced on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance made the announcement, which had been expected, during a speech at the annual March for Life in Washington. The policy change is the Trump administration's latest attack on what President Trump and his aides call ''woke ideology'' at home and abroad. It could affect more than $30 billion in foreign assistance.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance said that the change would cover all U.S. nonmilitary assistance to other nations.\par \par \uc2 The policy change was quickly denounced by liberal advocacy groups. The coalition Defend Public Health said in a statement it would ''coerce'' foreign groups ''into denying that transgender, nonbinary and intersex people exist, and undermine access to gender-affirming care and information, as well as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care.''\par \par \uc2 But the White House issued a statement declaring President Trump, who once called himself ''very pro-choice'' before entering national politics, ''the most pro-life president in history.''\par \par \uc2 The pre-existing Mexico City policy -- created and first declared by President \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  and announced in the Mexican capital in 1984 -- bars federal dollars from going to any foreign group that provides or promotes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even if those programs are paid for with other sources of financing.\par \par \uc2 Opponents of the policy call it the ''global gag rule.'' But conservatives note that money is fungible and that even U.S. tax dollars used for other purposes allow groups to use more of their other income sources for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related activities.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance said that it had been the policy of the Biden administration to ''export \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and radical gender ideology all around the world.''\par \par \uc2 He said the effect of expanding the Mexico City policy would be ''to protect life, to combat D.E.I. and the radical gender ideologies that prey on our children.''\par \par \uc2 ''All in all, we have expanded the Mexico City policy about three times as big as it was before, and we're proud of it, because we believe in fighting for life,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 The move is the latest in Mr. Trump's relentless campaign to stamp out what it denigrates as ''woke'' policies in both the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  and the private sector. His administration's actions have included changes to exhibits at national parks and museums, as well as threats to withhold federal dollars from colleges and universities that he accuses of following such policies.\par \par \uc2 It is also the latest curtailment of U.S. foreign aid by an administration that shut down the \uc2 U.S. Agency for International Development\uc2  last year, accusing the organization, which performed lifesaving humanitarian work on several continents, of supporting a liberal social agenda.\par \par \uc2 The State Department carried out the policy change by issuing three rules on Friday that were posted in the Federal Register, which said the policies were being implemented to ''ensure that foreign aid is aligned with administration policy and promotes human flourishing.''\par \par \uc2 ''The United States is concerned that, absent this rule, U.S. taxpayer funds may support radical gender ideology and organizations engaged in harm to women and children, and further, may do so in a manner that undermines the national laws and values of sovereign nations,'' one of the new rules states.\par \par \uc2 ''The promotion abroad of radical D.E.I. activities, and the ideology of discriminatory equity ideology that undergirds it, undermines the well-being and flourishing of foreign nations'' explains another.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Vance's remarks were met with enthusiastic cheers from the crowd on the National Mall. The March for Life is an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  event held annually in Washington since 1973, when the Supreme Court's Roe v. Wade decision legalized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. That ruling was overturned in 2022, but the event continues.\par \par \uc2 Sheryl Gay Stolberg contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Sheryl Gay Stolberg contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020260124em1o00044\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
