\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Newsom Nixes Louisiana Bid For Extradition Of a Doctor\b0\par\par\uc2 By Pam Belluck \par \uc2 709 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 January 2026\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 22\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The case, escalating the interstate battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is the second time Louisiana has criminally charged out-of-state doctors with sending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to Louisiana residents.\par \par \uc2 Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  of California said on Wednesday that his state would refuse to extradite a doctor who has been charged in Louisiana with providing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a resident of that state.\par \par \uc2 ''Louisiana's request is denied,'' Mr. Newsom, a Democrat, said in a statement. ''We will not allow extremist politicians from other states to reach into California and try to punish doctors based on allegations that they provided \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care services. Not today. Not ever.''\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Louisiana's attorney general, Liz Murrill, a Republican, released an indictment accusing a California \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, Dr. R\u233\'00\'E9my Coeytaux, of prescribing and mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to a woman who had found the telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  service the doctor worked for in October 2023, shortly after discovering she was pregnant. Gov. \uc2 Jeff Landry\uc2  of Louisiana, also a Republican, said hours later that he would sign an extradition order for the doctor.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Wednesday, Ms. Murrill called it ''appalling'' that California officials were ''openly admitting that they will protect an individual from being held accountable for illegal, medically unethical and dangerous conduct.''\par \par \uc2 Louisiana authorities learned about the case in March 2024 and issued an arrest warrant for Dr. Coeytaux in May 2024, according to affidavits from investigators and other documents that Louisiana released, which do not say who reported the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to state investigators.\par \par \uc2 The case is the latest escalation in the battle between states that has arisen since the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  eliminated the national right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2022. About a third of states, including Louisiana, currently have near-total bans on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . About 20 others have some type of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  shield law, including at least eight states -- California among them -- that explicitly refuse to cooperate with prosecutions, lawsuits or investigations against providers who supply \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication to states with bans.\par \par \uc2 California's telemedicine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  shield law was passed in September 2023 and took effect in January 2024. But almost immediately after the 2022 Supreme Court decision, Governor Newsom signed an executive order ''protecting state-held data and information from being used by out-of-state anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entities to target providers and patients, and declining requests received from other states to extradite health care providers for providing \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care services,'' the governor's office said in a statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Legal experts expect the battle over whether states need to honor one another's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws to eventually lead to a constitutional showdown that could reach the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, in testimony about medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before a Senate committee in Washington, Ms. Murrill said she was committed to prosecuting people who violate Louisiana's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws. ''Shield laws in some states protect providers from liability, and effectively nullify laws in our states,'' she said. ''Their purpose is to make it more difficult to sue or prosecute individuals in those states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs are prohibited.''\par \par \uc2 Dr. Coeytaux, who is charged with criminal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by means of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -inducing drugs, did not respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The documents released by Louisiana say that the woman, who is not named, received \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in the mail after supplying the telemedicine service with her personal information on a form and paying $150. She took the medication and terminated her pregnancy soon after, the documents said. From the package's postal tracking number, the investigators determined that the medication had been sent from a business in Dr. Coeytaux's name.\par \par \uc2 The case is the second time that Louisiana officials have sought criminal prosecution and extradition of an out-of-state doctor over the prescription of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. Last year, Louisiana sought to extradite a New York-based \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider, Dr. Margaret Carpenter, whom the state indicted on similar charges. Gov. \uc2 Kathy Hochul\uc2  of New York, a Democrat, has refused to agree to her extradition, citing the state's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  shield law. So far, Louisiana has not taken further action to try to extradite Dr. Carpenter.\par \par \uc2 Emily Cochrane contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Emily Cochrane contributed reporting.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020260118em1i0003l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
