\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Pence on Lonely Crusade Against Kennedy as  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Foes Avoid Fight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sheryl Gay Stolberg \par \uc2 1,333 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 13\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2 , who has taken different positions on the issue, has pledged to promote President Trump's anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda in a bid to get confirmed as health secretary.\par \par \uc2 Former Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , a longtime leader of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement, has taken up a lonely crusade to defeat the nomination of \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr.\uc2  for health secretary. His organization, Advancing American Freedom, is running ads against Mr. Kennedy. Mr. Pence has accused Mr. Kennedy of promoting ''\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand.''\par \par \uc2 His fellow \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents are not listening.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists descended on Washington on Friday to mark the 52nd anniversary of Roe v. Wade, the Supreme Court case that established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . President Trump addressed the crowd at the March for Life by video. Vice President \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  spoke in person. Mr. Kennedy, whose flip-flops on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have made many conservatives deeply uneasy, was not on the agenda -- and drew no mention.\par \par \uc2 But in a sign of how the right wing of the Republican Party is kowtowing to Mr. Trump -- and, perhaps, of the deepening break between Mr. Pence and the president -- leaders of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement are lining up behind Mr. Kennedy, or at least not openly opposing him.\par \par \uc2 Tim Chapman, who as president of Advancing American Freedom is leading Mr. Pence's campaign, said others in the conservative movement had told him privately that they agreed with the former vice president, but did not want to say so publicly. He said conservative leaders who failed to oppose Mr. Kennedy were abdicating their traditional role of pressuring party leaders on the issues the movement cared about.\par \par \uc2 ''His confirmation lays bare the real question right now about what the movement exists to do,'' Mr. Chapman said, adding, ''We have the freedom to plant the flag, and we know there are a lot of people who agree with us on this issue, and we hope that they'll join us.''\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Mr. Kennedy did not respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups and Christian conservatives have rallied around Mr. Trump since his 2016 run for office, when he promised to appoint Supreme Court justices who would overturn Roe. He succeeded; the decision was overturned in 2022.\par \par \uc2 At the march on Friday, Mr. Trump repeated false claims about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, vowing to ''stop the radical Democrat push for a federal right to unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand up to the moment of birth and even after birth.'' Mr. Vance called Mr. Trump ''the most pro-family, most pro-life American president of our lifetimes.'' The crowd roared.\par \par \uc2 In picking Mr. Kennedy as health secretary, Mr. Trump took a risk that he would alienate those supporters.\par \par \uc2 Instead, two leading anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups, Students for Life of America and Susan B. Anthony Pro-Life America, have avoided taking a position on Mr. Kennedy. The president of the march, Jeanne F. Mancini, has commended Mr. Kennedy. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  senators, including Tommy Tuberville of Alabama and \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  of Missouri, have embraced Mr. Kennedy, who reassured them that he would support Mr. Trump's anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda.\par \par \uc2 The man who forged that agenda during the first Trump administration, \uc2 Roger Severino\uc2 , has given Mr. Kennedy his full-throated support. As chief of the Office for Civil Rights within the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , Mr. Severino coined a new name for the agency: ''the Department of Life.'' He drafted the section on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Project 2025, \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 's pre-election blueprint for the Trump presidency.\par \par \uc2 ''I'm confident \uc2 Bobby Kennedy\uc2  will be confirmed and restore President Trump's stellar pro-life record from his first term,'' Mr. Severino said in a text message. ''He recognizes that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a tragedy and is surrounding himself with proven conservatives who will roll back Biden's radical and unpopular \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies with dispatch.''\par \par \uc2 Representative Robert B. Aderholt, Republican of Alabama and the chairman of the conservative House Values Action Team, said in an interview that while he understood Mr. Pence's reluctance, he was not concerned about Mr. Kennedy becoming health secretary. ''I have gotten the impression that his focus is not going to be so much on a pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  agenda,'' Mr. Aderholt said.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Kennedy's pronouncements on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been all over the map. In 2023, when he was running for president, Mr. Kennedy said he would support a federal ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the first trimester of pregnancy, then quickly backtracked. In May, while still a candidate, he posted a lengthy message on social media outlining his views.\par \par \uc2 ''I support the emerging consensus that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be unrestricted up until a certain point,'' he wrote. ''I believe that point should be when the baby is viable outside the womb.''\par \par \uc2 Now, in an effort to get confirmed, Mr. Kennedy is making specific policy commitments. According to Mr. Hawley, Mr. Kennedy pledged to reverse a rule issued by the Biden administration that protected patients who have had abortions, and also promised that ''all of his deputies'' at the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  would oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He also pledged to reinstate protections for health care workers who refuse to perform abortions because of their own objections, Mr. Hawley said on social media. And, Mr. Hawley said, Mr. Kennedy supports barring clinics funded by the 55-year-old Title X Family Planning Program from discussing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with patients. Federal law already bars Title X clinics from referring patients to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Tuberville also came away pleased after his meeting with Mr. Kennedy. ''He's telling everybody, 'Listen, whatever President Trump -- I'm going to back him 100 percent,''' he told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Pence has been on the outs with Mr. Trump since Jan. 6, 2021, when he presided over congressional certification of the 2020 election results as the Capitol was under assault from a pro-Trump mob.\par \par \uc2 His battle with fellow Republicans has turned personal. Katie Miller, a former Pence aide who is now Mr. Kennedy's spokeswoman, launched a stinging attack against her former boss on social media last week, accusing Mr. Pence of firing her when her daughter was 2 months old because her husband, \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , worked for Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 ''The American People clearly don't care a single iota what \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  has to say -- he resoundingly lost to President Trump,'' she wrote. ''Our country has moved on and it's time he does too. He's nothing but a footnote of American history.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump has been walking a delicate line on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Supreme Court overturned Roe. He has said the matter should be left to the states and has tried to steer clear of it. On Thursday, he pardoned 23 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protesters, including some convicted of blockading a clinic.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents have argued that if Mr. Kennedy is going to be health secretary, it is incumbent on the president to appoint other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes to key positions inside the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 . But they have stopped short of speaking out against Mr. Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 ''While I disagree with President Trump about whether \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a federal and state or a state-only issue, pro-life Americans can work with this team,'' \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , the president of Students for Life of America, wrote last month in The Federalist, a conservative online magazine.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, before the march, Mr. Pence's organization tried again to stir opposition to Mr. Kennedy, issuing a public letter emphasizing his rejection of vaccines and other unorthodox policies.\par \par \uc2 ''RFK Jr. has supported dangerous health-related conspiracy theories, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -on-demand, and increasing access to psychedelics,'' Mr. Chapman and another top adviser to Mr. Pence, Marc Short, wrote on social media. ''Senators must approach this selection with clear eyes and reject his nomination to be the Secretary of \uc2 Health and Human Services\uc2 .''\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250125el1p0003v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
